{
  "supported": true,
  "coverage": "partial",
  "coverage_explanation": "Exercises all three selections, initial stock depletion, release-triggered sales, a 1900ms short hold, repeated long-hold admin entry/exit, restocking while D7 remains held, rejection of restocking before the 2s threshold and outside admin, additive restocking of nonzero stock, zero payload, acceptance of payload 9999, newline framing, and 20ms idle framing. Exact sale counts and subsequent depletion checks expose unintended sales and incorrect inventory updates. Selection display values are checked, but item numbers equal their prices, so the required one-second alternation is not independently observable. Error-display presentation is not checked: the supported numeric display check is instantaneous and cannot soundly require a transient -1 to persist until a chosen snapshot. Audible sale duration and out-of-stock alarm activity remain unverified because their onset/cadence cannot be soundly captured by the available tone-at-an-instant checks without imposing additional timing choices. The 9999 inventory cap is implemented by the reference but not independently established by this finite suite; exhausting that stock would exceed the input-step budget. D13 has no specified operational meaning; only its authorized initial OFF state is checked. SysML ownership is outside the observable host API.",
  "assumptions": [
    "Uses the disclosed bench defaults: D2, D3, D4 and D7 are active-LOW buttons connected to GND and configured INPUT_PULLUP; D13 is an active-HIGH LED.",
    "The authoritative TM1637 mapping is CLK D8 and DIO D5; the passive audible output is D6.",
    "Serial frames use the disclosed named COMMAND INTEGER form, for example RESTOCK3 2 followed by newline, or terminated by at least 20ms of idle. Command codes are transport metadata, not invented alternative wire syntax.",
    "A selection persists until another selection button is pressed. Confirmation in admin mode does not sell; a long hold toggles mode once and its release does not sell.",
    "The public 250ms reaction allowance is used when scheduling commands after the 2000ms hold threshold. No particular debounce duration, startup selection, display formatting, alarm frequency, error persistence, or operational LED meaning is required by the checks.",
    "The reference chooses a 200ms error display, a 200ms out-of-stock alarm, a 2000Hz sale beep, and an admin-status LED. These are permissible witness choices, not additional candidate requirements."
  ],
